<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94824" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῐᾰδήφορ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκιάς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carrying a sunshade</i>, of the daughters of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέτοικοι</span> at Athens, who
				<i>carried sunshades</i> for the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κανηφόροι</span> in the Panathenaic procession,
				v.l.ib.<i><span class="en">
				134
			</span></i> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκιαδοφόροι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				174
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>shading, shady</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				16.18
			</span></i>.</div>
